ght: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CH50*</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">AH50*</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 40%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Classical pathway</strong></p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">C1q/r/s, C2, C4</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Low</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Normal</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 40%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Alternative pathway</strong></p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Factor B, factor D</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Normal</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Low</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 40%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Lectin pathway</strong></p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Mannose-binding lectin</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Normal</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Normal</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 40%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Terminal components</strong></p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">C3, C5-9</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Low</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 25%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Low</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"width: 40%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">*CH50 &amp; AH50 are measures of the function of the entire classical &amp; alternative complement cascades, respectively.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This boy's rapidly progressive illness with high fever and petechial rash raises strong suspicion for <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Neisseria meningitidis</strong></em> infection.\u00a0 The virulence of <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">N meningitidis</em> is due to the presence of a <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">polysaccharide capsule</strong>, which allows the organism to evade phagocytosis and immunoglobulin attachment.\u00a0 Because of these adaptations, initial control of infection is primarily mediated by activation of the <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-aoxlh6r01grv55wvgx441tpx\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-aoxlh6r01grv55wvgx441tpx\">alternative complement cascade</a>, which is triggered when autoactivated C3 interacts with the surface of the bacteria and amplifies.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Activation of the alternative pathway results in generation of the following:</p><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start inline\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">C3b:\u00a0 a powerful opsonin that binds to complement receptor 1 on erythrocytes and phagocytes, which increases phagocytosis by reticuloendothelial monocytes</p></li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start inline\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">C3a and C5a:\u00a0 potent anaphylatoxins that recruit immune cells and drive a strong inflammatory response</p></li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start inline\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Membrane attack complexes</strong> (MACs):\u00a0 composed of the terminal complement proteins (C5-9), MACs generate a channel in the bacterial surface, leading to osmotic lysis of the organism</p></li></ul><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">MACs are the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">most important initial defense</strong> against encapsulated bacteria because they operate at high efficiency despite the presence of a capsule.\u00a0 Therefore, patients with <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">deficits</strong> in any of the terminal complement proteins that generate the MAC are at very high risk for <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">recurrent encapsulated bacterial infections</strong> (as seen in this patient).\u00a0 Laboratory evaluation of these patients will show <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">reduced activity</strong> of the classical <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(CH50)</strong> and alternative <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(AH50)</strong> complement cascades because all 3 complement pathways (classical, alternative, lectin) terminate in the generation of MACs.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choices B and C)</strong>\u00a0 Deficiency in complement proteins unique to the classical cascade (eg, C1q/r/s, C2, C4) will result in low CH50 and normal AH50 levels.\u00a0 In contrast, deficiency in complement proteins unique to the alternative cascade (eg, factor B, factor D) will result in normal CH50 and low AH50 levels.\u00a0 This patient's recurrent <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">N meningitidis</em> infections are more characteristic of a terminal complement component deficiency.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 Patients with a defect in the lectin complement pathway (eg, mannose-binding lectin) will have normal CH50 and AH50 levels.\u00a0 Additional evaluation with the mannose-binding lectin test can usually reveal the presence of this abnormality.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Initial control of encapsulated bacteria is largely reliant on the formation of membrane attack complexes (MACs) due to activation of the alternative complement cascade.\u00a0 Patients with deficiency in the proteins that generate MACs (C5-9) are at high risk for recurrent encapsulated bacterial infection; evaluation will show reduced activity of the classical (CH50) and alternative (AH50) complement cascades.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Initial control of encapsulated bacteria is largely reliant on the formation of membrane attack complexes (MACs) due to activation of the alternative complement cascade.  Patients with deficiency in the proteins that generate MACs (C5-9) are at high risk for recurrent encapsulated bacterial infection; evaluation will show reduced activity of the classical (CH50) and alternative (AH50) complement cascades.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b", "subject": "Immunology", "system": "Allergy & Immunology", "topic": "Complement deficiency", "category": "Immune deficiencies", "peerCorrect": 39.0}